# Specs

A ticket is read once by a worker in a cold checkout and by an owner deciding whether it is worth doing. About three hundred words. Every line serves one of them or goes. Template: `spec/features/_template/ticket.md`.

- **Title.** `FNNN · what becomes true`. The folder carries the slug; the lane carries the status.
- **Outcome.** Two to four sentences: what someone can do or see afterwards. Product terms, no mechanism.
- **Scope.** Boundary and starting seam as a lead, not the edit list.
- **Out of scope.** Only nearby work someone would plausibly do by mistake.
- **Acceptance.** One observable behavior or check per line, verifiable with a command or a look. Not "tests pass". A line holding several checks is several lines.
- **Notes.** Decisions and open questions only. Never progress.

Never put a status line, date, author tag, bare feature number, prerequisites, phases, or implementation shape in the ticket.

`planned/` → `active/` when work begins → `done/YYYY-MM/` or `dropped/YYYY-MM/` when terminal. The number is stable for life. The folder keeps the ticket, notes, numbered `review-N.md`, and `outcome.md`. Delete a file that stops being true.

`spec/build.md` is TRACK / NOW / NEXT / PROVEN. Update it in the same change that moves a folder. PROVEN keeps the last ten, then one month line.

```
Bad:  Acceptance — tests pass and spawn is fast and the tab focuses.
Good: Acceptance — `limen spawn --tab` prints the job id before the worker process starts.
```
